				<Callout tone="blue" title="A Mac, Linux or WSL2, with Docker running">
					<svg slot="icon" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="2" y="4" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="M8 21h8"/><path d="M12 18v3"/></svg>
					<p>Postgres runs in a container on your laptop, so Docker Desktop (or colima) has to be up. On Windows, set up WSL2 with a normal (not root) user, turn on Docker Desktop's WSL integration for that distro, and install Node through nvm inside WSL. Don't rely on Windows' own node or pnpm: they leak into WSL through the PATH. <a href="/get-started/#windows">The Windows steps</a>.</p>
